abstract: >-
  Firms that each ask the same AI model what to produce can end up running a
  cartel without ever talking to each other. This repository measures when
  that happens in one-shot Cournot markets with no messages between firms,
  and what stops it from outside the firm's own prompt: a line in the model
  provider's system prompt, a regulator monitoring the firm's prompt or the
  model's reply, audits, and rivals on other models. Written for the Apart
  Research AI Collusion Research Sprint, 23 to 25 October 2026.
